The test vehicle approaches the intersection at target speed V1. Cyclists waiting to cross the pedestrian crossing are positioned on the left/right side of the left vertical lane, maintaining a distance D from the lane centerline. The cyclist crosses the pedestrian crossing from the left/right side of the current lane at speed V2. During the test vehicle's left turn through the intersection, the time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the cyclist to reach the collision point.